description:
**lawcheck output/JSON polish** (small, one commit):
- mutant `detail` is always the literal `"Error:"` (`lawcheck.ts:1032` keeps only line 1) → keep the first `- expected`/`Location` lines;
- `Report` omits `maxNat` → add it (reproducibility); add `schema: 1` to the JSON;
- zero-arg calls shown as `D.two` instead of `D.two()`; `~` marks dropped (`Heap.sort(U32, U32.is_le, …)` should show `~U32`) — fix the term printer;
- skip messages say `(v0.2)` although this is 0.2.0 → drop the version tag from messages;
- with `--json`, errors print as plain text on stderr → emit `{"error": {...}}` on stdout with the same exit code;
- README: macOS binaries downloaded from GitHub are quarantined → one line `xattr -d com.apple.quarantine ./lawcheck-darwin-*`.
Acceptance: tests for detail, schema, printing; `bun test tools/lawcheck` green.

---
Rules (AGENTS.md, "Working the beads"): bun only; never delete files; never publish, `bend link`,
tag or release unless this bead is labelled `release`; never weaken a statement, test, assertion or
gate to get green (if stuck: keep the bead open and `br comments add <id> "<what you tried + exact
error>"`); lean comments (AGENTS.md "Comments"). Close with `br close <id> --reason "<acceptance
commands + their last output lines>"`.
